<title>UK: MoD may delay Eurofighter missile contract-paper.</title>
<headline>MoD may delay Eurofighter missile contract-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Ministry of Defence is considering postponing its decision on a planned 900 million pound ($1.46 billion) missile system for the new Eurofighter aircraft, the Financial Times newspaper said on Monday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the decision on who will supply the Eurofighter missiles may be postponed in the run-up to the general election in Britain, which must be held before the end of May.</p>
<p>Hughes of the U.S. and a European partnership led by British Aerospace, including Matra of France and Daimler-Benz of Germany are in competition for the project.</p>
</text>
